    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5505632/assistant-professor-health-kinesiology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Health & Kinesiology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Health & Kinesiology Salary See Position Description Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600525 Home Org Health and Kinesiology Opening Date 10/05/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary This tenure-track position involves a range of duties and responsibilities essential to the role. Key responsibilities include: •Teaching undergraduate/graduate courses in Kinesiology, with a focus in exercise science, strength and conditioning, and biomechanics. •Assist with developing the program to meet the needs of the job market as well as pre-professional pathways. •Advising and mentoring students. •Supervising student field experiences. •Pursuing a research agenda that results in publications and extramural support. •Collaborating with field-based colleagues. •Providing service to the department, college, university, and profession. •Incorporating the use of career related AI within courses. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Teaching: Teaching undergraduate/graduate courses in Kinesiology, with a focus in exercise science, strength and conditioning, and biomechanics. Utilize both face-to-face and online course delivery methods, integrating innovative and evidence-based teaching strategies. Supervise student field experiences, internships, and applied learning opportunities. Maintain regular office hours and provide academic support to students. Research/grant writing: Develop and sustain a research agenda in kinesiology. Publish findings in peer-reviewed journals and present at professional conferences. Mentor students in research projects, theses, and presentations. Pursue external funding opportunities to support research and departmental initiatives. Service: Providing service to the department, college, university, and profession. Contribute to professional organizations and accreditation processes (e.g. program review, curriculum development). Support community outreach and partnerships that advance health, fitness, and kinesiology. Collaborate with faculty across disciplines and with field-based colleagues to enhance program offerings. Advising: Serve as an academic advisor/mento to students. Guide students in professional development, graduate school preparation, and career pathways. Support students seeking professional certificates. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Doctorate in Kinesiology, Exercise Science, or related field. ABD will be considered. The ability to teach both face-to-face and online course delivery methods. Preference will be given to those applicants who have prior teaching experience at the college level using both face-to-face traditional and online course delivery. Ability to work effectively with colleagues and students in a collaborative environment. Demonstrate potential for scholarly activity. Desired Qualifications: Commitment to excellence in teaching and scholarship; Experience and proficiency teaching at the university level; Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate coursework in kinesiology; including but not limited to, exercise physiology, biomechanics, exercise prescription, and strength and conditioning, among others; ACSM or CSCS certification; Blackboard LMS experience; Accreditation experience. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Demonstrated knowledge and skills in kinesiology regarding strength and conditioning, exercise physiology, and biomechanics. Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. Ability to implement effective and innovative teaching strategies. Ability to perform academic research in a degree area of specialty. Demonstrated commitment to service to the university, profession, and community. Physical Requirements: Able to lift 40 lbs and be able to perform a variety of physical tasks including lifting, bending, stooping, squatting, stair climbing, and walking between buildings. Standing or sitting for extended periods while teaching or in office hours. Job Conditions: Office, Classroom, Field experiences, laboratory. Pay Range: Commensurate Required Documents: These documents are required for the application to be considered complete. Teaching Philosophy Curriculum Vita Resume Cover Letter Finalists for this position are subject to a criminal history background check, employment history check, and off-list reference checks. Applicants are required to sign an authorization for release of prior employment records to Lamar University. We will only contact prior employers and off-list references for finalists. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance . Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Doctorate in Kinesiology, Exercise Science, or related field OR ABD? Yes No 02 Do you have the ability to teach both face-to-face and online course delivery methods. Preference will be given to those applicants who have prior teaching experience at the college level using both face-to-face traditional and online course delivery? Yes No 03 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5511830/assistant-professor-geospatial-engineering": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Geospatial Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Geospatial Engineering Salary See Position Description Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600527 Home Org Civil Engineering Opening Date 10/09/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at Lamar University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in geospatial engineering. This is a nine-month appointment with an anticipated start date of August 2027 (Fall 2027). We seek an energetic educator and researcher with expertise in remote sensing, geographic information systems (GIS), surveying and geomatics, LiDAR, three-dimensional visualization, or digital twins, and the ability to connect these technologies to civil engineering practice. Teaching is a central responsibility: the successful candidate will teach multiple courses each semester and bring enthusiasm to classroom, field, and laboratory instruction. Research interests may include remote sensing and spatial analytics; LiDAR and point-cloud processing; three-dimensional mapping; digital twins of infrastructure and built environments; infrastructure monitoring; and integration of geospatial data with engineering models. Applications may span transportation, construction, industrial facilities, coastal infrastructure, environmental monitoring, and water resources. Expertise in every listed area is not expected. The successful candidate will pursue external funding and engage industry, public agencies, and academic partners on challenges relevant to Southeast Texas and beyond. The department welcomes AI, emerging sensing technologies, and advanced visualization in instruction and research, with attention to data quality, uncertainty, and sound engineering judgment. The anticipated annual workload is 40% teaching, 50% research, and 10% service. Teaching: Teach multiple undergraduate and/or graduate courses each semester, with an anticipated assignment of two courses per semester (2-2). Primary areas include surveying and geomatics, GIS, remote sensing, and geospatial applications in civil engineering. Develop advanced instruction in LiDAR, three-dimensional visualization, digital twins, or related topics within the candidate's expertise. Create engaging field, laboratory, and computational experiences connecting measurement and spatial analysis to engineering practice. Advise and mentor students and contribute to curriculum development and assessment. Research: Establish and sustain an externally funded research program in geospatial engineering. Pursue funding, publish scholarly work, and mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers. Build partnerships with industry, public agencies, and academic collaborators to address regional and broader engineering needs through remote sensing, spatial analysis, visualization, or related technologies. Applications may include infrastructure monitoring, construction, transportation, coastal systems, environmental monitoring, and water resources. Maintain research activity consistent with the assigned workload and tenure expectations. Service: Contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service, including curriculum improvement, accreditation, recruitment, outreach, and initiatives supporting student retention and career readiness. Build relationships that create opportunities for student projects and professional development. Essential Job Functions Establish and sustain an externally funded research program in geospatial engineering. Pursue funding, publish scholarly work, and mentor undergraduate and graduate researchers. Build partnerships with industry, public agencies, and academic collaborators to address regional and broader engineering needs through remote sensing, spatial analysis, visualization, or related technologies. Applications may include infrastructure monitoring, construction, transportation, coastal systems, environmental monitoring, and water resources. Maintain research activity consistent with the assigned workload and tenure expectations. Teach multiple undergraduate and/or graduate courses each semester, with an anticipated assignment of two courses per semester (2-2). Primary areas include surveying and geomatics, GIS, remote sensing, and geospatial applications in civil engineering. Develop advanced instruction in LiDAR, three-dimensional visualization, digital twins, or related topics within the candidate's expertise. Create engaging field, laboratory, and computational experiences connecting measurement and spatial analysis to engineering practice. Advise and mentor students and contribute to curriculum development and assessment. Contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service, including curriculum improvement, accreditation, recruitment, outreach, and initiatives supporting student retention and career readiness. Build relationships that create opportunities for student projects and professional development. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: An earned Ph.D. in civil engineering or a closely related field, with expertise in geospatial methods applied to civil engineering, is required by the time of appointment. Prior teaching experience and preparation to teach multiple courses each semester in geospatial engineering, with a commitment to energetic instruction, student success, and undergraduate and graduate mentoring. Strong communication and collaboration skills; and a Professional Engineer (PE) license or a demonstrated pathway and commitment to obtaining licensure. Expertise in GIS and remote sensing, with relevant capability in LiDAR, surveying, three-dimensional visualization, or digital twins; a research and publication record appropriate to career stage; and potential to establish an externally funded research program. Desired Qualifications: Professional experience applying geospatial technologies to civil engineering practice, infrastructure planning, design, construction, or asset management. Experience collecting and processing field data using surveying equipment, GNSS, LiDAR, or aerial remote sensing platforms. Active Professional Engineer (PE) licensure. Experience leading field instruction and mentoring student design or research projects. Experience with three-dimensional modeling, digital twins, geospatial programming, AI, spatial analytics, or interactive visualization. Applications to hydrologic or hydraulic modeling are also welcome. Experience developing research proposals, participating in sponsored projects, or building industry and public-agency partnerships. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Teach surveying and geomatics, GIS, remote sensing, and geospatial applications with enthusiasm and develop engaging classroom, field, laboratory, and computational instruction. Develop an externally funded geospatial engineering research program that connects data collection, analysis, and visualization to engineering decisions. technical concepts clearly and integrate emerging technologies while emphasizing data quality, uncertainty, and engineering judgment. Mentor students, collaborate with regional industry and public agencies, and contribute to departmental, university, and professional service. Physical Requirements: Able to lift 25 lbs and be able to perform a variety of physical tasks including lifting, bending, stooping, squatting, stair climbing and walking between buildings. Job Conditions: Work is performed in a combination of academic, laboratory, office, and outdoor field environments. The position may involve exposure to varying weather conditions, uneven terrain, surveying equipment, remote sensing technologies, and other field-related hazards while conducting research or supervising instructional activities. Compliance with university safety policies and applicable laboratory and field safety procedures is required. The position may require occasional evening or weekend hours to accommodate teaching, research, fieldwork, student activities, and university events. Occasional travel may be required for field research, professional conferences, research collaborations, and other university-related activities. Pay Range: Commensurate Finalists for this position are subject to a criminal history background check, employment history check, and off-list reference checks. Applicants are required to sign an authorization for release of prior employment records to Lamar University. We will only contact prior employers and off-list references for finalists. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have an earned Ph.D. in civil engineering or a closely related field, with expertise in geospatial methods applied to civil engineering, is required by the time of appointment. Yes No 02 Do you have prior teaching experience and preparation to teach multiple courses each semester in geospatial engineering, with a commitment to energetic instruction, student success, and undergraduate and graduate mentoring. Yes No 03 Do you have strong communication and collaboration skills; and a Professional Engineer (PE) license or a demonstrated pathway and commitment to obtaining licensure. Yes No 04 Do you have expertise in GIS and remote sensing, with relevant capability in LiDAR, surveying, three-dimensional visualization, or digital twins; a research and publication record appropriate to career stage; and potential to establish an externally funded research program. Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5513016/assistant-professor-graphic-design-art-design": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Graphic Design Art & Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Graphic Design Art & Design Salary See Position Description Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600486 Home Org Art Opening Date 10/12/2026 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Department of Art & Design at Lamar University, a NASAD-accredited program committed to excellence in art and design education, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Graphic Design. We seek an engaged educator and active practitioner whose work reflects contemporary graphic design across print, digital, interactive, and emerging media. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses across the curriculum, including typography, brand identity, UX/UI, and portfolio development, as well as foundation courses as needed. The ideal candidate combines a strong grounding in design fundamentals and conceptual thinking with the ability to prepare students for a rapidly evolving creative field. We are particularly interested in candidates who situate graphic design within broader professional, technological, and disciplinary contexts, and who can guide students in developing effective, industry-relevant design solutions. The candidate should demonstrate fluency in industry-standard tools (Adobe Creative Cloud, Mac platforms), along with UX/UI prototyping tools and emerging technologies, including AI-assisted design processes. As an R2 institution, Lamar University values faculty who maintain an active and sustainable program of creative, professional, or scholarly work. The successful candidate will contribute to a culture of teaching excellence, student mentorship, and ongoing creative activity. Application Materials Cover letter Curriculum vitae Teaching philosophy Designer or research statement Portfolio of professional work (PDF (9MB or less), including 20 images of representative artworks, including titles, dates, materials, and relevant details; may include a link to a website. Portfolio of student work (PDF (9MB or less), including 15-20 relevant examples Sample syllabus designed by the candidate Names and contact information for three references Unofficial transcript Finalists may be asked to provide additional materials. Special Note: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Teaching and Instruction Teach undergraduate courses in graphic design, including typography, brand identity, UX/UI, and introductory design. Develop course materials, syllabi, and instructional content aligned with current industry practices. Assess student performance and provide feedback to support academic and professional development. Maintain regular office hours and provide academic advising and mentorship. Research and Creative Activity Maintain an active program of creative, scholarly, or professional work appropriate to the discipline. Produce exhibitions, publications, or other recognized creative outputs. Engage in ongoing professional development and contribute to the advancement of the field. Service and Program Support Participate in departmental, college, and university committees. Contribute to curriculum development and program assessment aligned with contemporary design practices. Support student recruitment, retention, and program growth initiatives. Assist with departmental events, exhibitions, and outreach activities. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications MFA, MDes, or terminal degree in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, or related field. Ability to teach all levels of Graphic Design, and select Foundation Design courses as needed. Ability to teach industry-standard software, including the Adobe Creative Cloud, and knowledge of Mac-based platforms. Evidence of ongoing creative, professional, or scholarly activity. Ability to teach undergraduate courses across graphic design curriculum, including typography, brand identity, UX/UI, and portfolio development. Proficiency with industry-standard design tools, including Adobe Creative Cloud applications. Working knowledge of Macintosh platforms. Demonstrated record or potential for ongoing creative, professional, or scholarly activity. Desired Qualifications Two years of college-level teaching experience Professional practice or research in areas such as b.rand identity, typography, UX/UI, web, motion, or interactive design. Experience with web-based tools, and/or AI-assisted design workflows. Demonstrated potential for sustained creative or scholarly output. Experience mentoring students toward internships, exhibitions, and career readiness. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Teach all levels of undergraduate Graphic Design and Foundation Design courses as needed. Mentor students in senior thesis, portfolio development, and career preparation. Maintain an active creative, professional, or research practice. Contribute to and/or lead curriculum development aligned with contemporary design practices. Support recruitment, retention, and program growth. Participate in service at the department, college, and university levels. Physical Requirements: Work is performed in a standard academic environment and requires the ability to sit, stand, walk, use a computer, and communicate effectively. May involve lifting and carrying light materials (up to 20 pounds). Visual acuity sufficient for reviewing materials and delivering instruction is required. Job Conditions: Work is performed in classroom, studio, and computer lab environments. Responsibilities include use of specialized art and design equipment and software. Duties may require extended periods of standing, as well as occasional evening or weekend commitments for critiques, exhibitions, recruitment activities, and departmental events. Pay Range: Commensurate Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Finalists for this position are subject to a criminal history background check, employment history check, and off-list reference checks. Applicants are required to sign an authorization for release of prior employment records to Lamar University. We will only contact prior employers and off-list references for finalists. Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a MFA, MDes, or terminal degree in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, or related field (or higher)? Yes No 02 Do you have the ability to teach all levels of Graphic Design, and select Foundation Design courses as needed? Yes No 03 Do you have the ability to teach industry-standard software, including the Adobe Creative Cloud, and knowledge of Mac-based platforms? Yes No 04 Can you provide evidence of ongoing creative, professional, or scholarly activity? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5521791/assistant-professor-nutrition": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Nutrition",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Nutrition Salary See Position Description Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600541 Home Org Nutrition, Hospitality & Human Serv Opening Date 10/19/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Assistant Professor of Nutrition is a tenure-track faculty position within the Department of Nutrition, Hospitality & Human Services. This role is responsible for teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in nutrition across multiple modalities, contributing to curriculum development, and supporting program accreditation requirements. The faculty member is expected to maintain an active research and scholarly agenda, including mentoring student research, disseminating findings, and pursuing external funding. In addition, the position provides academic advising and mentorship to students, contributes to program and departmental initiatives, and engages in service at the department, college, university, and professional levels. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Teaching: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in nutrition in all modalities. Develop and revise online courses using the Quality Matters review process and update on-campus courses using best teaching practices for the discipline. Maintain professional certifications, if applicable. Develop, implement, and monitor student performance outcomes through ongoing assessment. Hold regular office hours and maintain campus presence to ensure accessibility and engagement with students. Scholarly & Creative Activities: Maintain an active research agenda with dissemination of findings in through scholarly publications and presentations. Collaborate with faculty in research, outreach, and pursuit of external funding opportunities. Mentor undergraduate and graduate research projects. Service: Advise undergraduate students in the nutrition program. Serve on Departmental, College, and University committees. Provide service to the community and to the nutrition and dietetics profession. Perform other departmental and program duties as assigned. Collaborate with other departments and units across campus to strengthen interdisciplinary initiatives. Engage in community outreach aligned with program and university goals. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral Degree or ABD with expected graduation May 2027 in Nutrition from an accredited institution. RDN credential required. Demonstrated ability or potential for teaching is important. Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills for working with students, staff, faculty, and administration. Commitment to creating and sustaining an environment of student support and success. Active involvement in professional organizations within the field of specialty. Demonstrated ability to work in a collaborative and innovative environment. Desired Qualifications: Experience with ACEND requirements in academic coursework. Strong interest and proven competence in research and scholarship. Research experience with demonstrated scholarship via first-authored publications Teaching experience at the College or University level with experience in curriculum development and course design utilizing the Quality Matters process. Practical nutrition and dietetics experience as a Registered Dietitian Nutritionist. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: The ability to translate knowledge into essential practice skills for nutritionists and registered dietitian nutritionists. Provide instruction in nutrition courses across modalities (in-person, hybrid, and online). Develop/revise online applied nutrition courses utilizing the Quality Matters review process. Participate in planning, review, and evaluation of bachelor’s and master’s programs, including certificates and concentrations. Develop, implement, and monitor student performance outcomes through assessment. Advise and mentor nutrition students. Collaborate with other departments and units across campus. Report curriculum and course issues to appropriate program coordinators; report all other issues to the Department Chair. Serve on Departmental, College, and University committees as assigned. Physical Requirements : Ability to articulate clearly in lectures and discussions. Ability to stand or sit for extended periods while teaching. Ability to move around classrooms and laboratories as needed. Job Conditions : Deliver courses both face-to-face and online. Work within department offices to support the department, college, and university mission focused on the success of both on-campus and online students. Pay Range : Commensurate Finalists for this position are subject to a criminal history background check, employment history check, and off-list reference checks. Applicants are required to sign an authorization for release of prior employment records to Lamar University. We will only contact prior employers and off-list references for finalists. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Doctoral Degree or ABD with expected graduation May 2027 in Nutrition from an accredited institution? Yes No 02 Do you have a RDN credential? Yes No 03 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5063837/campus-safety-officer-part-time": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Campus Safety Officer (Part-Time) Salary $14.31 Hourly Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Hourly Worker Job Number 202500062 Home Org Police Department Opening Date 08/31/2025 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Non-Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary Lamar University is seeking dependable and professional Campus Safety Officers to support the safety and welfare of our students, faculty, staff, visitors, and property. Officers provide service, information, and assistance as needed, deter crime through a visible presence, assist victims, prepare reports, and observe and report safety issues. This role serves as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) as defined by the Clery Act. Essential Job Functions What You’ll Do – Position Responsibilities Perform safety and security duties on Lamar University property Preserve safety by interceding to deter or prevent crime Investigate non-criminal incidents and detect security or safety issues Prepare accurate written reports of incidents and non-criminal activities Provide credible testimony in court when required Assist and support victims of crime Provide aid and assistance to students, faculty, staff, and visitors Observe and report potential hazards or safety issues Perform other duties as assigned Minimum and Desired Qualifications Education: High School Diploma or GED Must be eligible to drive a University-owned or leased vehicle Ability to complete a six-month probationary period upon hire Strong written and oral communication skills Ability to effectively use handcuffs, OC spray, radios, patrol vehicles, computers, and investigative and surveillance equipment. Knowledge of emergency medical procedures, first aid, and CPR techniques Strong problem-solving skills with the ability to provide credible reports and testimony Must be able to work any shift (days, nights, weekends, and holidays) Physical Requirements Ability to drive, walk, run, stand, stoop, climb, crouch, push, pull, lift, grasp, and carry items Must have good physical condition, vision, hearing, and use of arms and legs Ability to work outdoors in varying weather conditions Preferred Qualifications Enrolled in classes at Lamar University Previous experience in a safety or security role Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a High School Diploma or GED? Yes No 02 Are you eligible to drive a University-owned or leased vehicle? Yes No 03 Are you able to work flexible shifts, including days, nights, weekends, and holidays? Yes No 04 Do you have prior experience in safety or security work? Yes No 05 Are you trained in CPR, first aid, or emergency medical response? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5071529/campus-safety-officer-full-time-pooled": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer (Full Time - Pooled)",
      "description": "Campus Safety Officer (Full Time - Pooled) Salary $29,759.00 Annually Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202500129 Home Org Police Department Opening Date 09/05/2025 FLSA Non-Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary To provide service, information and aid to all citizens as circumstances require, assist and support victims of crime when directed by a supervisor, deter crime through constant uniformed presence, take non-criminal reports, and observe and report safety issues on campus. Serves as a Campus Security Authority as defined by the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act). Responsible for safety and welfare of students, faculty, staff, visitors, and all property under the control and jurisdiction of Lamar University. Exercises independent judgment and discretion within the limits prescribed by the Rules and Regulations of the Board of Regents, institutional rules and regulations, and the Lamar University Police Departmental policies and procedures. Essential Job Functions To perform security and safety duties on the property of Lamar University. Preserve the safety and security by interceding, to prevent or deter crime. Investigate non-criminal incidents to detect safety or security issues, and lost property. Prepare various written reports narrating incidents, supplemental information, and non-criminal activities. Give credible and accurate testimony in the criminal courts of this state and the United States -if required. Provides assistance and support to the victims of crime, and to all students, faculty, staff and visitors to the Lamar University campus. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED. EQUIPMENT: Required: Proficient with all equipment utilized in the performance of assigned duties, to include but not be limited to handcuffs, oleoresin capsicum spray (OC), public safety vehicles, communications equipment, computers, investigative and surveillance equipment. Desired Qualifications: Enrolled in classes at Lamar University to complete degree. Experience in a safety and security position, with similar duties. Supplemental Information ACCURACY: Proficiency in all phases of duties performed. Must demonstrate logical and effective problem solving ability. Must be able to provide creditable testimony in a court of law. PHYSICAL CAPABILITIES: Duties involve driving, walking, running, standing, stooping, climbing, crouching, pushing, jumping over, pulling, carrying, reaching above head, lifting, lowering, hand-wrist and elbow motion, grasping, and holding. Good physical condition and vision, ability to hear and speak and full use of arms and legs. WORKING CONDITIONS: Usual: Exposure to outside weather conditions. May be required to work either day or night on any one of three shifts with varying days off and on holidays. Work may involve a degree of hazard. WHO WE ARE: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. BENEFITS: Health, dental & vision insurance? Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents. Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays.? To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a High School diploma or GED? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5361820/associate-director-student-recruitment": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Student Recruitment",
      "description": "Associate Director, Student Recruitment Salary $58,739.00 - $76,361.00 Annually Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600286 Home Org Area Recruiting Opening Date 08/24/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Associate Director of Admissions, Recruitment provides strategic leadership for the university’s recruitment efforts across freshman, graduate, and international student populations. This position is responsible for developing, implementing, and assessing comprehensive recruitment and yield strategies to meet institutional enrollment goals. The Associate Director supervises and develops Assistant Directors, ensuring effective execution of recruitment initiatives and alignment with university priorities. Essential Job Functions Develop, implement, and continuously refine a comprehensive recruitment strategy and annual plan that aligns with institutional enrollment goals across freshman, graduate, and international student populations; ensure effective execution through Assistant Directors and recruitment staff. Provide direct supervision, coaching, and performance management for Assistant Directors by establishing clear expectations, monitoring progress toward goals, and fostering a high-performing and collaborative team environment . Utilize Slate to monitor funnel performance, assess the effectiveness of recruitment initiatives, and adjust strategies to meet enrollment targets. Recommend and implement improvements to recruitment communications, marketing strategies, and student engagement efforts to effectively articulate the university’s value proposition and attract prospective students aligned with enrollment goals. Partner with academic colleges, graduate programs, international programs, marketing, and student services to align recruitment messaging, improve yield strategies, and enhance the prospective student experience from inquiry through enrollment. Provide strategic oversight and direction for recruitment events, travel, special programs, and key initiatives; ensure alignment with enrollment priorities, efficient resource utilization, and consistent execution across student populations. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree. 4 years of progressive recruitment, admissions, and/or higher education experience required. Other relevant leadership experience may substitute. Desired Qualifications: Master’s degree in Leadership, Business Management, Higher Education, or similar preferred. Prior management and leadership experience preferred. Experience and knowledge of Slate or other CRM systems preferred. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Leadership & Team Development: Ability to lead, coach, and develop professional staff, including managing through others and fostering accountability, collaboration, and high performance. Data-Informed Strategy: Ability to analyze data to inform strategy, monitor performance, and adjust tactics to meet enrollment goals. Strategic Communication & Messaging: Ability to communicate effectively across various audiences through clear, persuasive written, verbal, and presentation skills. Judgement & Decision-Making: Ability to exercise discretion and sound judgement in handling sensitive student information, personnel matters, and organizational priorities. Collaboration & Cross-Functional Engagement: Ability to build strong working relationships across divisions (academic colleges, graduate programs, international offices, marketing, etc.) to support recruitment goals. Adaptability & Innovation: Demonstrated flexibility and a proactive mindset in responding to changing enrollment trends, technologies, and student needs. Physical Requirements: Ability to lift, load, and transport recruitment materials, displays, and other equipment up to 35 pounds. Job Conditions: Ability to travel and work a varied schedule with flexible hours, including some weekends and evenings. Enrollment in and successful completion of MGMT 3311 Leadership Essentials within the first six months of employment. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance. Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents. Paid time off, vacation, sick, and holidays. To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Bachelor’s degree? Yes No 02 Do you have at least 4 years of progressive experience in recruitment, admissions, and/or higher education? Yes No 03 If not, do you have other relevant leadership experience that could substitute for this requirement? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5488534/assistant-professor-physiology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Physiology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Physiology Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600485 Home Org Biology Opening Date 09/18/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary This is a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in the Department of Biology. The appointee is expected to establish a vigorous, externally funded research program, publish in peer-reviewed journals and teach effectively across the biology curriculum with special emphasis on Animal Physiology related courses. Additional responsibilities include service to the department, university, and discipline. The successful candidate will also involve undergraduate and graduate students in research. Preference will be given to candidates who have postdoctoral experience and whose research expertise can be leveraged towards advanced courses in Physiology utilizing molecular tools. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions 1.Implement effective teaching strategies: Teach Biology courses as assigned. Develop course materials and contribute to curriculum development. 2.Maintain an active research agenda that includes publication of research papers in peer-reviewed journals and/or submission of research grants: Conduct cutting edge research in the area of expertise. Publish findings in peer-reviewed journals and present at professional conferences. Supervise and mentor students. Secure external funding through grants to support research initiatives. 3.Actively participate in academic service at the department, college, and university levels: Serve the department, college and university as needed. Assist in recruitment and retention of biology students. Contribute to the academic and professional community through participation in relevant organizations and initiatives. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: A PhD in Biology or related field. An established record of publications in peer-reviewed scientific journals that are listed by the Web of Science. Willingness to develop and teach courses in area of research expertise and also Anatomy and Physiology, Upper-level Physiology. Desired Qualifications: Research background that can be leveraged towards advanced courses in Physiology. Postdoctoral research experience. Evidence of strong potential to secure external research funding. Evidence of strong potential to mentor students in research. Evidence of strong potential to teach high-quality courses across the biology curriculum. Experience in presenting research results at high-profile conferences. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Strong ability to perform research in area of specialty. Expected success in securing extramural funding. Strong ability to teach high-quality Biology courses across the curriculum. Demonstrated commitment to service to the university, profession, and community. Excellent interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. Physical Requirements: Able to lift 25 lbs and be able to perform a variety of physical tasks including lifting, bending, stooping, squatting, stair climbing and walking between buildings. Job Conditions: Standard academic work schedule, with occasional evening or weekend responsibilities to meet research, teaching, service, or administrative deadlines. Position requires on-campus teaching with potential remote collaboration for research activities. Required Documents: The following documents are required for your application to be considered complete. Teaching Philosophy Curriculum Vita Research Statement Cover Letter Three Letters of Recommendation Finalists for this position are subject to a criminal history background check, employment history check, and off-list reference checks. Applicants are required to sign an authorization for release of prior employment records to Lamar University. We will only contact prior employers and off-list references for finalists. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a PhD in Biology or related field? Yes No 02 Do you have an established record of publications in peer-reviewed scientific journals that are listed by the Web of Science? Yes No 03 Do you have a willingness to develop and teach courses in area of research expertise and also Anatomy and Physiology, Upper-level Physiology? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5504971/assistant-professor-speech-hearing": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Speech & Hearing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Speech & Hearing Salary See Position Description Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600513 Home Org Speech and Hearing Services Opening Date 10/05/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Assistant Professor is a tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Speech and Hearing responsible for teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, providing clinical education and supervision, and maintaining an active program of research and scholarly activity. The position mentors and advises undergraduate and graduate students and contributes service to the department, college, university, profession, and community. The faculty member supports the academic, research, and service missions of the department and university through effective teaching, scholarship, student development, and professional engagement. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Teaching and Clinical Education: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in assigned areas, including clinical education and supervision. Develop and deliver course content, assess student learning and performance, maintain appropriate academic standards, and fulfill related instructional responsibilities. Research and Scholarly Activity: Maintain an active program of scholarly and creative activities, including conducting research, publishing and disseminating findings, participating in professional scholarly activities, and pursuing external funding opportunities as appropriate. Student Mentoring and Advising: Mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students regarding academic progress, research activities, professional development, and career goals. University, Professional, and Community Service: Provide service to the department, college, university, profession, and community through committee participation, professional activities, community engagement, and other appropriate service responsibilities. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent research doctoral degree. Eligibility for licensure in the State of Texas. Evidence of potential for excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Prior teaching experience in higher education. Desired Qualifications: Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service appropriate to academic rank. Certificate of Clinical Competence (CCC-A) from the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association. Active holder of or eligible to obtain appropriate Texas state professional licensure at the time of hire. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Knowledge of effective teaching methodologies, research practices, and clinical education and supervision appropriate to the discipline. Knowledge of scholarly research, publication, and dissemination practices appropriate to the discipline. Ability to mentor undergraduate and graduate students and support their academic, research, professional, and career development. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills necessary for effective teaching, collaboration, and stakeholder engagement. Ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, students, clinical partners, community stakeholders, and interdisciplinary teams. Ability to conduct scholarly and creative activities and contribute to the research mission of the department, college, and university. Ability to provide effective academic and professional service to the department, college, university, profession, and community. Physical Requirements: The successful candidate must be able to communicate effectively in classroom, laboratory, and clinical environments; stand, walk, and move between instructional, office, research, and clinical settings; and sit for extended periods while performing teaching, research, administrative, and computer-based work. The position requires the ability to operate standard office equipment, computers, audiovisual systems, and instructional technology; observe and assess student performance in academic and clinical settings; and occasionally lift, carry, or move instructional materials, equipment, and supplies weighing up to 25 pounds. Job Conditions: Work is performed in classroom, laboratory, clinical, and office environments and requires frequent interaction with students, staff, faculty, and community partners. The position may require weekend activities related to teaching, student supervision, community outreach, and a variety of academic settings. Pay Range: Commensurate Finalists for this position are subject to a criminal history background check, employment history check, and off-list reference checks. Applicants are required to sign an authorization for release of prior employment records to Lamar University. We will only contact prior employers and off-list references for finalists. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Ph.D. or equivalent research doctoral degree? Yes No 02 Do you have the Eligibility for licensure in the State of Texas? Yes No 03 Do you have prior teaching experience in higher education? Yes No 04 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
