    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5477059/post-doctoral-researcher": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Researcher",
      "description": "Post Doctoral Researcher Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600471 Home Org Inst Energy & Petro Ind Eng Researc Opening Date 09/09/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Postdoctoral Research Associate will support applied research conducted through the Center for Midstream Management and Science . The position will contribute to multiple projects involving midstream energy systems, pipelines, leak detection, emissions, instrumentation, laboratory measurements, and data analysis. The research will be conducted in the lab and in the field. The postdoctoral researcher will help design and conduct experiments, operate research equipment, analyze data, prepare technical deliverables, and support the development of new research methods. Assignments may change as CMMS develops new projects and industry partnerships. The position is therefore intended for a researcher who can work across several technical areas and quickly learn new systems. This is a temporary position with an initial appointment of one year. The position may be renewed for one additional year, contingent upon satisfactory performance and continued approval, for a maximum appointment of two years. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Applied Research and Project Execution: Conduct applied research in support of CMMS-sponsored and faculty-led projects. Design experiments, develop research methods, and evaluate new technologies. Manage assigned activities according to project schedules, objectives, and sponsor requirements. Laboratory and Field Measurements: Operate, calibrate, and troubleshoot laboratory and field measurement equipment. Conduct measurements involving leak detection, gases, emissions, sensors, and other project variables. Maintain experimental records and follow established safety and quality procedures. Data Analysis and Technical Development: Process, analyze, and interpret experimental and operational data. Develop scripts, models, software, or visualization tools needed for research projects. Evaluate data quality, measurement uncertainty, and system performance. Research Collaboration and Project Support: Work with CMMS faculty, staff, students, and industry partners on multidisciplinary projects. Contribute to technical reports, publications, proposals, presentations, and sponsor deliverables. Provide technical guidance to students and assist with laboratory and project activities. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Terminal degree in engineering, physics, chemistry, or a closely related STEM discipline at the level of PhD or DE. Experience conducting experimental or applied research in an academic, laboratory, field, or industrial setting. Ability to plan experiments, collect and analyze data, and document research methods and results. Experience preparing technical reports, presentations, or peer-reviewed publications. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively to multidisciplinary research teams. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Strong background in mathematics up to partial differential equations in three dimensions in solving the Helmholtz Equation in different coordinate systems, including cylindrical symmetries and applications of Bessel functions. Ability to manage multiple research tasks and meet project schedules and sponsor requirements. Willingness to travel for conducting research in the field across the Nation. Ability to present results at workshops, symposia, and conferences. Desired Qualifications: Experience with laboratory measurement systems such as mass spectrometry, gas chromatography, gas analyzers, or vacuum equipment. Experience with sensors, instrumentation, data-acquisition systems, or automated experimental equipment. Experience with programming, signal processing, statistical analysis, machine learning, or scientific data visualization. Experience conducting field tests or working with industry-sponsored research projects. Familiarity with laboratory safety, calibration procedures, quality control, and experimental uncertainty. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Ability to design, conduct, and troubleshoot laboratory and field experiments. Ability to learn and operate unfamiliar instruments, software, and research systems. Strong analytical skills and the ability to interpret complex experimental data. Ability to document procedures, code, equipment configurations, and research findings clearly. Ability to collaborate with faculty, students, technical staff, industry partners, and project sponsors. Ability to oversee research projects for undergraduate and graduate students. Strong organizational skills and attention to experimental quality and safety. Ability to publish results across the spectrum of trade journals to high-impact journals. Physical Requirements: Able to lift 25 pounds and be able to perform a variety of physical tasks including lifting, bending, stooping, squatting, stair climbing, and walking between buildings. Job Conditions: Work is typically performed in a lab or office environment. Occasional visits to field testing sites will be required. Flexibility in working hours may be needed during experimental deployments or system upgrades. Required Documents: Please note you MUST have these documents attached to your application to be considered complete. Cover Letter with a link to your PhD thesis Resume/Curriculum Vitae Transcripts from PhD program Research Statement 3 Letters of Reference, one of which must come from your PhD advisor Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students , Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120 -degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders,demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance . Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Terminal degree in engineering, physics, chemistry, or a closely related STEM discipline at the level of PhD or DE? Yes No 02 Do you have experience conducting experimental or applied research in an academic, laboratory, field, or industrial setting? Yes No 03 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5504833/instructor-political-science": {
      "title": "Instructor, Political Science",
      "description": "Instructor, Political Science Salary See Position Description Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600439 Home Org Political Science Opening Date 10/05/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The instructor in Political Science will teach face to face and on-line sections of POLS 2301: Intro to American Gov’t I and POLS 2302: Intro to American Gov’t II. Both courses have an American government and Texas government component. Well qualified faculty may be asked to teacher upper level or graduate courses based on qualifications and departmental need. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Teach undergraduate Political Science courses, including POLS 2301: Introduction to American Government I and POLS 2302: Introduction to American Government II, in face-to-face and online formats. Develop and deliver course content that incorporates American and Texas government principles and achieves established learning outcomes. Assess and evaluate student learning through examinations, assignments, projects, and other instructional methods; maintain accurate academic records; provide timely feedback; and submit grades in accordance with university policies and deadlines. Support student success by maintaining regular office hours, responding to student inquiries, providing academic guidance, and fostering an engaging and productive learning environment. Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities, remain current in the discipline and instructional methods, and teach upper-level or graduate Political Science courses as assigned based on qualifications and departmental needs. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in political science or public administration. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate courses in American Government,including federal and Texas government topics. Desired Qualifications: Ph. D. in Political Science or Public Administration. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Effective teaching skills. Effective verbal/written communication skills. Effective interpersonal and organizational skills. Physical Requirements: Standing for extended periods of teaching. Job Conditions: Work is performed in a classroom, office, and online instructional environment and requires the ability to teach face-to-face and virtual courses using instructional technology and learning management systems. The position requires effective verbal and written communication skills, regular interaction with students, faculty, and staff, and the ability to prepare instructional materials, evaluate student performance, maintain academic records, and meet established deadlines. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required to support instructional, departmental, or university activities. The employee must be able to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while teaching, grading, and performing administrative tasks, and must comply with all applicable university policies, accreditation standards, and state and federal regulations. Pay Range: Commensurate Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Master’s degree in political science or public administration? Yes No 02 Do you have the demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate courses in American Government,including federal and Texas government topics? Yes No 03 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5514862/manager-of-marketspace-and-fabrication-labs": {
      "title": "Manager of Marketspace and Fabrication Labs",
      "description": "Manager of Marketspace and Fabrication Labs Salary $46,827.00 - $60,875.00 Annually Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600488 Home Org Sponsored Program Administration Opening Date 10/13/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Manager of Makerspace and Fabrication Labs supports teaching and experiential learning through the safe and effective operation of Lamar University's Makerspace and fabrication facilities. The position manages day-to-day Makerspace operations, equipment maintenance and access, student-worker activities, inventory, safety practices, and training programs related to digital and manual fabrication. The Manager provides technical guidance and instruction to students, faculty, and staff; supports instructional and research activities; and ensures fabrication equipment and facilities are maintained in a safe, organized, and operational condition. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Makerspace Programming, Training and Student Engagement: Create and administer programmatic content centered around Makerspace fabrication equipment. Conduct individual and group training sessions on the safe and appropriate use of Makerspace equipment. Conduct student-centered events promoting the Makerspace and its resources. Evaluate new equipment and programs that align with the needs of the campus community. Advise students regarding equipment use and appropriate safety precautions. Ensure users receive appropriate training and authorization before independently operating Makerspace equipment. Student Worker Supervision: Provide direct supervision of student workers, including coaching, performance management, and development. Plan and assign workloads and provide day-to-day oversight of student-worker activities. Ensure student workers adhere to applicable university, departmental, safety, and operational policies and procedures. Equipment, Facility, and Inventory Operations: Maintain, clean, schedule, and ensure the operational condition of equipment within the Makerspace and affiliated areas. Establish and maintain appropriate safety precautions for Makerspace equipment and facilities. Create and maintain operational service manuals and regular equipment-maintenance schedules. Manage and safeguard inventory, consumables, supplies, and equipment. Perform fixed-asset inventory checks as required. Facility Access, Safety and Compliance: Manage access to the Makerspace in the Science & Technology Building and its secure rooms in a compliant and systematic manner. Coordinate with Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) and Risk Management regarding inspections, safety requirements, and regulatory compliance. Maintain appropriate access controls and safety procedures for Makerspace facilities and equipment. Faculty Instructional and Research Support: Provide laboratory and fabrication support for faculty performing instructional and research activities. Assist with access to appropriate equipment and Makerspace resources in support of instructional and research projects. Facilitate the availability of consumables, equipment, and other materials necessary to support faculty activities. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in a science, technology, engineering, or mathematics (STEM)-related field. Minimum of two years of experience in a fabrication, makerspace, machine shop, or similar technical environment. Working knowledge of laboratory and shop safety practices. Desired Qualifications: Degree in an engineering or technology-related field. Hands-on experience with HAAS CNC equipment. Prior supervisory or team leadership experience, including training others in the use of equipment. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Knowledge of and demonstrated ability to safely operate manufacturing and fabrication equipment, including lathes, mills, CNC equipment, grinders, shapers, drill presses, MIG/TIG welding equipment, plasma tables, and related equipment. T echnical aptitude and ability to troubleshoot and resolve equipment and operational issues independently. Knowledge of training programs and effective instructional methods. Effective verbal and written communication skills with the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and staff. Knowledge of laboratory, fabrication, and shop safety requirements and practices. Ability to collaborate with faculty and students on instructional and research projects. Ability to maintain a safe, organized, and active makerspace environment. Ability to work effectively both independently and as a member of a team. Physical Requirements: With or without accommodation, this position requires the performance of physical tasks associated with the operation and maintenance of equipment in a fabrication shop. Some activities may require working outdoors in full sun, rain, heat, or cold. The position also frequently requires desk-based computer work, telephone use, clear verbal communication, and adequate listening comprehension. Must be able to lift up to 25 pounds and perform physical activities including lifting, bending, stooping, squatting, stair climbing, and walking between buildings. Job Conditions: This position may require occasional evening and/or weekends to meet university and departmental needs. Who We Are : Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Bachelor's degree in a science, technology, engineering, or mathematics (STEM)-related field? Yes No 02 Do you have a minimum of two years of experience in a fabrication, makerspace, machine shop, or similar technical environment? Yes No 03 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5515368/sr-academic-advisor": {
      "title": "Sr. Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Sr. Academic Advisor Salary $41,809.00 - $54,352.00 Annually Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600506 Home Org Undergraduate Advising Center Opening Date 10/13/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Academic Advisor at Lamar University plays a crucial role in supporting students throughout their academic journey, with a particular focus on high-risk students. This position involves guiding students through the entire matriculation cycle, from initial enrollment to graduation, ensuring they receive the necessary support and resources to succeed. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Student Support and Advising: Provide comprehensive support to students, focusing on high-risk individuals, through initial enrollment, course completion, and re-enrollment each term. Offer personalized advising to help students develop academic plans and achieve their educational and career goals. Academic Planning and Course Selection: Assist students in selecting appropriate courses, developing academic plans, and understanding degree requirements. Utilize degree audit reports and predictive analytics to monitor and guide students' academic progress. Compliance and Policy Implementation: Ensure that university policies and state mandates are followed in advising and enrollment processes. Advise students on academic policies, procedures, and requirements. Data Management and Reporting: Track and report student interactions, success data, and progress. Maintain accurate student records using advising systems and technologies and provide regular updates to supervisors. Outreach and Engagement: Participate in university and recruitment events, present at New Student Orientation, and engage in ongoing assessment activities. Collaborate with Enrollment Management offices to support student matriculation and reenrollment decisions. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree. 2 years experience in academic advising or a similar role within higher education. Excellent communication skills. Interpersonal skills and the ability to build and maintain positive relationships. Excellent time-management skills. Desired Qualifications: Master’s degree Previous mentorship of advisors and advising procedures. Knowledge of literature and best practices related to undergraduate advising and student retention initiatives. Familiar with advising tools, such as Banner, Degree Works, and Navigate. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Ability to maintain a high level of dependability, professionalism, and customer service. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including active listening and the ability to present information clearly and professionally. Ability to build relationships with students, faculty and staff. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Ability to assess student needs and provide appropriate guidance and solutions. Familiar with Microsoft Office and student information systems or advising software. Develop and expand academic advising strategies. Physical Requirements: The physical requirements for his position require the ability to sit for extended periods as much of the work involves desk and computer tasks. Proficiency in using a computer, including typing and navigating software programs along with the ability to read and interpret documents, emails, and other written material. Job Conditions: This position is in an office setting, with occasional meetings and events around campus. Standard work hours are typically Monday through Friday, with some flexibility required for evening and weekend events. Travel is generally limited to on-campus activities, conferences, or professional development opportunities. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Bachelor's degree? Yes No 02 Do you have 2 years experience in academic advising or a similar role within higher education? Yes No 03 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5521223/instructor-criminal-justice": {
      "title": "Instructor, Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Instructor, Criminal Justice Salary See Position Description Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600509 Home Org Sociology Soc Work Crim Just Opening Date 10/19/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Instructor of Criminal Justice is responsible for providing high-quality undergraduate instruction and fostering student success through effective teaching, advising, mentoring, and academic engagement. This nine-month, full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position teaches Criminal Justice courses in face-to-face and online learning environments, develops and assesses course materials and student learning outcomes, and supports students' academic, professional, and career development. The position contributes to curriculum coordination, program assessment, student recruitment and retention efforts, and departmental, college, and university service activities. The successful candidate will maintain current knowledge of developments within the criminal justice field, engage in professional development, collaborate with faculty, staff, students, and community partners, and support the mission of the Department of Criminal Justice and Lamar University through excellence in teaching, service, and student-centered learning. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Teach undergraduate Criminal Justice courses in face-to-face and online learning environments; develop and deliver course materials; assess student learning outcomes; provide academic advising, mentoring, and career guidance; maintain office hours; and support student success, retention, and professional development. Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, accreditation-related activities, instructional planning, student recruitment and retention initiatives, and other departmental academic priorities. Participate in departmental, college, and university service activities; maintain current knowledge of developments within the criminal justice field through professional development; and support community engagement, agency partnerships, internships, and other activities that enhance student learning and career readiness. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree or higher from an accredited institution. A minimum of 18 graduate semester credit hours in criminal justice, criminology, or a closely related discipline sufficient to meet faculty credentialing requirements. Academic preparation sufficient to teach a broad range of undergraduate Criminal Justice courses. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate Criminal Justice courses. Ability to use instructional technologies and learning management systems to support teaching and learning. Desired Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Criminal Justice, Criminology, or a closely related field. A minimum of two years of previous college or university teaching experience in both face-to-face and online learning environments. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Teaching and Instructional Effectiveness. Student Advising and mentoring. Online teaching and instructional technology. Commitment to Academic integrity and professional ethics. Physical Requirements: Ability to perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Requires the ability to communicate effectively in individual and group settings, including delivering lectures, facilitating classroom discussions, advising students, and participating in meetings. Must be able to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while teaching classes, conducting office hours, preparing instructional materials, and performing other faculty responsibilities. The position requires the ability to move between classrooms, offices, meeting locations, and other campus facilities; operate a computer and standard office and instructional equipment; and occasionally lift, carry, or transport instructional materials, equipment, or supplies weighing up to 25 pounds. Job Conditions: Work is primarily performed in classrooms, offices, meeting spaces, and other academic environments and requires regular on-campus presence to support teaching, office hours, student advising, departmental meetings, service activities, and other university responsibilities. Teaching assignments may include face-to-face and online instruction and may be scheduled during daytime, evening, or other designated class periods based on departmental needs. The position involves frequent interaction with students, faculty, staff, community partners, and external stakeholders, as well as occasional local travel for professional development, recruitment, community engagement, experiential learning opportunities, and other university-related functions. Work is conducted in a professional academic setting utilizing standard office and classroom equipment and involves minimal exposure to adverse environmental conditions. Pay Range: Commensurate Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have Master’s degree or higher from an accredited institution? Yes No 02 Do you have a minimum of 18 graduate semester credit hours in criminal justice, criminology, or a closely related discipline sufficient to meet faculty credentialing requirements? Yes No 03 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply"
    }
